<title>INDIA: India's 95/96 sugar output at 16.45 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>India's 95/96 sugar output at 16.45 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's 1995/96 (October-September) sugar production rose to 16.452 million tonnes against 14.6 million in the same period in 1994/95, an industry official said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The final estimate for 1995/96 sugar ouput is at 16.452 million tonnes,&quot; Shanti Lal Jain, director-general of Indian Sugar Mills Association (ISMA) told Reuters.</p>
<p>ISMA, the apex organisation of India's sugar mill owners, is due to hold its annual general meeting on Friday.</p>
<p>--Sambit Mohanty, New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
